WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.175 --> 00:00:03.055
This is it ladies and gentlemen: The Final Episode

00:00:03.055 --> 00:00:06.035
Castle Rock season 1 and boy is it gonna

00:00:06.035 --> 00:00:08.475
cost some controversy. But before we get into that

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.755
I just wanted to say

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.835
a huge Thank You to those who've watched and subcribed

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.685
My channel has exploded because of you guys and I

00:00:15.685 --> 00:00:17.440
hope that you stayed tuned even

00:00:17.445 --> 00:00:20.305
if I do another show because you know i'm gonna be back here

00:00:20.305 --> 00:00:22.155
for season 2. The finale begins

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.935
with the warden Lacy and the kid back in the water tank.

00:00:24.935 --> 00:00:27.945
Lacy prepares a nutritions lunch of an apple,

00:00:27.945 --> 00:00:30.935
the fruit used to attempt Adam in the Garden of Eden,

00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:34.055
bread, the body of Christ, and a moon pie

00:00:35.655 --> 00:00:36.655
 

00:00:37.005 --> 00:00:39.015
He uses the walking stick to move the

00:00:39.015 --> 00:00:41.665
tray, as to not get touched before getting of his gloves

00:00:41.665 --> 00:00:43.755
and smoking a Malboro,,

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.740
the same brand warden Porter examinated in episode 1.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.245
Judging by his parking spot being painted

00:00:49.245 --> 00:00:52.255
over the bucket of cigarettes and Lacy's overall appearance

00:00:52.255 --> 00:00:55.305
this scene likely happened shortly before the events

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:58.215
of episode 1. The events which set this story emotion.

00:00:58.215 --> 00:01:01.145
Lacy brings out a gun and pointed out the kid

00:01:01.145 --> 00:01:03.935
clearly torned he should pull the trigger or not

00:01:03.935 --> 00:01:06.255
the kid even leans in closer almost

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:09.140
as if tatting him, but Lacy doesn't go through with it

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:12.060
as his told us in voiceovers the previous episodes

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.080
there's still doubt whether what his doing

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.700
is right. And this idea

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.640
of doubt, not knowing for certain

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.040
who or what something is

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.695
plays a key role in understanding the ending

00:01:21.695 --> 00:01:23.835
but we'll get to that in a bit. At Shawshank

00:01:23.835 --> 00:01:26.385
warden Porter watches as it meets a

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:28.765
transfer to new prisons. Shawshank is

00:01:28.765 --> 00:01:31.305
shutting down after its handling of recent scandals

00:01:31.305 --> 00:01:33.705
specifically Zalescki, God rest his soul.

00:01:33.705 --> 00:01:35.835
Notice the axe placement here

00:01:35.835 --> 00:01:38.545
a nice note to Jackie who's seen in the next scene having

00:01:38.545 --> 00:01:40.665
put one to the back of Gord's head, who

00:01:40.665 --> 00:01:43.535
also happens to be a blood relative to Jack Torrance.

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:46.655
"Here's Johnny!" After the events of episode 9

00:01:46.655 --> 00:01:49.635
the story picks up of where we left off in 8

00:01:49.635 --> 00:01:52.315
Wendell is back in Castle Rock and Henry rushes off

00:01:52.315 --> 00:01:54.835
in search of Ruth after getting a call from

00:01:54.835 --> 00:01:57.345
Appleton, but we find out where Ruth is

00:01:57.345 --> 00:02:00.445
staying at the top of Pangborn bridge, just like she did in

00:02:00.445 --> 00:02:02.845
episode 5. The kid tells Molly that he needs

00:02:02.845 --> 00:02:04.315
her help to convince Henry to

00:02:04.315 --> 00:02:07.075
go out to the woods with him. The two of them need to be together

00:02:07.075 --> 00:02:08.715
to get through the rift

00:02:08.715 --> 00:02:11.515
and set everything right before the sound of the skisma disappear

00:02:11.515 --> 00:02:13.595
trapping him there for good.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.000
Now if you believe the kid is evil you can look

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:19.060
at this in different way, that the kid is merely using Henry

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:19.860
and his ability to

00:02:19.865 --> 00:02:22.645
hear the skisma in order to travel to a different

00:02:22.645 --> 00:02:25.335
world to spread his evil. The kid tells Molly

00:02:25.335 --> 00:02:28.105
for Henry to meet him at Harmony Hill Cemetery

00:02:28.105 --> 00:02:30.685
which those of you who ever read Salem's Lot

00:02:30.685 --> 00:02:33.385
is where Mike Rianson digs up on dead Danny Clig.

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:35.965
Finally, Molly asked what she was like on

00:02:35.965 --> 00:02:38.615
the other side to which the kid responds: "Happier".

00:02:38.615 --> 00:02:41.355
Happier if you believe him but also dead

00:02:41.355 --> 00:02:42.075
Molly

00:02:42.075 --> 00:02:45.155
lives a voicemail to Henry telling him she needs to talk to him when his

00:02:45.155 --> 00:02:48.125
car has been bombard by birds like the one who slanted

00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:51.495
into the bus and he crushes into a pile of bricks and woods

00:02:51.495 --> 00:02:53.875
talked about a rough day. After the tilted credits Molly

00:02:53.875 --> 00:02:56.655
finds Ruth on the bridge and tries to cost her down

00:02:56.655 --> 00:02:59.665
Ruth tells Molly she saw this moment many times

00:02:59.665 --> 00:03:01.735
but when Molly tells her about how she had left

00:03:01.735 --> 00:03:04.365
with Alan in the alternate time line she said

00:03:04.365 --> 00:03:05.755
"First time you've said that"

00:03:05.755 --> 00:03:08.965
Suggesting that something is different about what's happening now

00:03:08.965 --> 00:03:11.545
warden Porter comes home and finds one of the kid's soap

00:03:11.545 --> 00:03:14.625
carvings in her image. Back in 1991

00:03:14.625 --> 00:03:17.395
young Henry and Matthew adventured into the woods

00:03:17.395 --> 00:03:19.185
Henry is caught in a lie by his father

00:03:19.185 --> 00:03:21.515
about hearing the skisma. Matthew tells

00:03:21.515 --> 00:03:23.345
his son that Ruth has been cheating and

00:03:23.345 --> 00:03:25.495
once she's gone the two of them can live pure

00:03:25.495 --> 00:03:28.135
in the cathedral of God's voice. When Henry

00:03:28.135 --> 00:03:30.405
asks what his gonna do he recites a line from

00:03:30.405 --> 00:03:32.465
"Romans" 6:23

00:03:32.465 --> 00:03:34.795
"For the wages of sin, death."

00:03:34.795 --> 00:03:37.335
implying that Matthew is going to kill Ruth

00:03:37.335 --> 00:03:38.935
for her adultering saying

00:03:38.935 --> 00:03:40.405
"She's left me no choice."

00:03:40.405 --> 00:03:42.915
Henry runs from his father as we transition back to

00:03:42.915 --> 00:03:44.755
present day. Dead birds covered in snow

00:03:44.755 --> 00:03:47.565
and Henry is woken by a passer by who blames it on

00:03:47.565 --> 00:03:50.495
global warming

00:03:50.505 --> 00:03:52.335
 

00:03:52.335 --> 00:03:54.845
Wendell walks into the forest and comes across the crime scene

00:03:54.845 --> 00:03:56.085
of the RV. Willie is there

00:03:56.085 --> 00:03:59.025
likely indicating that he was the one who killed Odin

00:03:59.025 --> 00:04:01.895
or he probably would've rushed off unless he's trying to set up

00:04:01.895 --> 00:04:03.805
Henry. He sees Wendell but doesn't

00:04:03.805 --> 00:04:06.585
say him anything just give him a creepy stare

00:04:06.585 --> 00:04:08.755
Henry arrives back to Ruth to find that she's okay.

00:04:08.755 --> 00:04:11.785
She seem to can't find her queen chess piece.

00:04:11.785 --> 00:04:12.575
The last time

00:04:12.575 --> 00:04:15.455
we saw it was on the table near the front door at the end of

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:18.365
episode 7. Molly tells Henry about her time with the kid

00:04:18.365 --> 00:04:19.795
but does a terrible job

00:04:19.795 --> 00:04:22.525
at convincing him to meet him at the cemetery

00:04:22.525 --> 00:04:25.455
First, by saying all the bad things that happened around him

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:28.265
coupled with the fact that Matthew and her died there

00:04:28.265 --> 00:04:31.120
well for Molly in the alternate time line. Henry is being

00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:33.135
rational here saying that the best course

00:04:33.135 --> 00:04:34.975
of action would be to turn in the kid.

00:04:34.975 --> 00:04:37.255
Henry goes to the police station were he finds

00:04:37.255 --> 00:04:38.345
his son, who tells him

00:04:38.345 --> 00:04:41.175
he also heard the skisma which is why he came back

00:04:41.175 --> 00:04:44.135
Henry is detained with an eye witness, Willie, he tells them

00:04:44.135 --> 00:04:47.005
that Henry had an argument with Odin a few days ago,

00:04:47.005 --> 00:04:49.925
Odin who is now dead. Warden Porter goes to Molly

00:04:49.925 --> 00:04:51.195
with the soap carving

00:04:51.195 --> 00:04:54.225
asking where the kid is and telling her that Lacy was right

00:04:54.225 --> 00:04:56.575
the kid is the Devil. Molly recognize it

00:04:56.575 --> 00:04:59.445
as similar with the one that kid carved and left on her diagrama

00:04:59.445 --> 00:05:02.485
Porter than shifts mumbling something to herself

00:05:02.485 --> 00:05:05.055
almost as something is taking over her

00:05:05.055 --> 00:05:06.915
kindly like something took over

00:05:06.915 --> 00:05:09.685
Zaleski. She turns to the street and strike killed by

00:05:09.685 --> 00:05:12.365
one of the Shawshank buses. Back at the station

00:05:12.365 --> 00:05:15.365
Henry is question by the police. His DNA was found

00:05:15.365 --> 00:05:18.125
in the RV and it's not looking good for him getting out of jail

00:05:18.125 --> 00:05:19.145
any time soon.

00:05:19.145 --> 00:05:22.335
Henry uses his one phone call to call Molly who's being

00:05:22.335 --> 00:05:24.005
questioned by the death of warden Porter

00:05:24.005 --> 00:05:26.835
next to a bus of restless inmates.

00:05:26.835 --> 00:05:27.645
He tells Molly

00:05:27.645 --> 00:05:30.575
that he's rescind to the fact that he's gotta be put away for a long time

00:05:30.575 --> 00:05:33.545
and asks her to take Wendell to his mother in Boston and

00:05:33.545 --> 00:05:35.945
to keep driving to start a new life.

00:05:35.945 --> 00:05:38.255
Molly then tells Henry where the kid is

00:05:38.255 --> 00:05:40.955
Harmony Hill Cemetery where we see him waiting

00:05:40.955 --> 00:05:43.995
Henry is brought to jail while the cops descend on the kid

00:05:43.995 --> 00:05:46.995
arresting him in front of his grave: The Deaver Boy.

00:05:46.995 --> 00:05:49.825
Remember, according to the kid in the alternate time line

00:05:49.825 --> 00:05:52.795
he's the son of Ruth and Matthew who didn't passed away in childbirth.

00:05:52.795 --> 00:05:54.255
 

00:05:54.255 --> 00:05:57.265
Molly tries to consult Wendell telling him his dad didn't do anything wrong.

00:05:57.265 --> 00:05:59.905
But even Wendell seems to have his doubts

00:05:59.905 --> 00:06:02.675
he asks "Does it have something to do with the sound in the woods?"

00:06:02.675 --> 00:06:04.235
The kid is brought into the

00:06:04.235 --> 00:06:06.365
jail where Henry is held and proceeds to tell

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:08.345
him that he's not supposed to be there

00:06:08.345 --> 00:06:09.625
in this timeline

00:06:09.625 --> 00:06:12.565
If he doesn't get back to the woods in time he could be stuck

00:06:12.565 --> 00:06:15.605
there forever and things will only get worse.

00:06:15.605 --> 00:06:18.705
More people will die. But Henry isn't buying it.

00:06:18.705 --> 00:06:20.815
He asks what would have happened to Ruth in the

00:06:20.815 --> 00:06:23.595
kids timeline if she hadn't left. To which the kid says:

00:06:23.595 --> 00:06:25.835
"Matthew would've shoot her" than recites the line

00:06:25.835 --> 00:06:28.685
from Romans 6:23

00:06:28.685 --> 00:06:30.695
a line that only Henry would know.

00:06:30.695 --> 00:06:32.395
At the Deaver home Jackie puts Ruth to bed

00:06:32.395 --> 00:06:34.165
which I thought was a bit weird bacause

00:06:34.165 --> 00:06:37.075
I don't think that Jackie and Ruth have been into a scene together

00:06:37.075 --> 00:06:39.775
unless Molly told her to take care of Ruth off screen

00:06:39.775 --> 00:06:41.295
while she deals with Wendell.

00:06:41.295 --> 00:06:43.465
The guards make Henry go to the kid cell

00:06:43.465 --> 00:06:45.405
to make room for the Shawshank prisoners

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:47.875
that where in the bus that ran over warden Porter.

00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:49.975
They recognize the kid calling him by

00:06:49.975 --> 00:06:51.095
his nick name:

00:06:51.095 --> 00:06:54.165
Nick Cage which Zaleski told us about in an earlier episode.

00:06:54.165 --> 00:06:56.845
Ruth grabs the knight chess piece and holds it to her heart

00:06:56.845 --> 00:06:59.025
The piece symbolizing her knight

00:06:59.025 --> 00:07:01.485
Alan Pangborn, it is also the last

00:07:01.485 --> 00:07:04.375
shot of Sissy Spacek we see this season

00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:06.535
 

00:07:06.535 --> 00:07:09.435
One of the prisoners stabs another one with a shank resulting in the wounded

00:07:09.435 --> 00:07:10.465
prisoner to be let out.

00:07:10.465 --> 00:07:12.895
He grabs one of the guard's gun, shoots

00:07:12.895 --> 00:07:14.525
the rest and freeze the other prisoners.

00:07:14.525 --> 00:07:17.545
All when Henry looks at the kid in other shaw

00:07:17.545 --> 00:07:20.625
as if he's orchestrating the whole thing. The keys

00:07:20.625 --> 00:07:23.625
convenient slide into the cell which the kid uses to take

00:07:23.625 --> 00:07:26.205
Henry upstairs where all the other cops have been shoot

00:07:26.205 --> 00:07:28.415
Henry finds Willie clinging to life

00:07:28.415 --> 00:07:31.335
with his final words he says "Don't go out there"

00:07:31.335 --> 00:07:34.375
as the kid points a gun on Henry saying "we have to go"

00:07:34.375 --> 00:07:37.125
and if you believe the kid's story he told Molly

00:07:37.125 --> 00:07:39.555
in episode 9 can you blame him he's been

00:07:39.555 --> 00:07:42.435
trapped in this world for 27 years about to lose

00:07:42.435 --> 00:07:44.665
his only way home wouldn't you do the same?

00:07:44.665 --> 00:07:47.285
or perhaps he's needing Henry for more nefarious porpoises

00:07:47.285 --> 00:07:49.125
 

00:07:49.125 --> 00:07:51.955
Explosions and mayhem glitter the street of Castle Rock as the escape

00:07:51.955 --> 00:07:54.895
prisoners roam free. Henry is taken to the forest where

00:07:54.895 --> 00:07:57.025
the sound of the skisma gets louder and he

00:07:57.025 --> 00:07:59.865
experiences more and more flashbacks.

00:07:59.865 --> 00:08:01.415
Young Henry having run away from his father

00:08:01.415 --> 00:08:04.285
almost falls over the edge of Castle Rock bluff

00:08:04.285 --> 00:08:05.795
He carefully walks backwards

00:08:05.795 --> 00:08:08.445
avoiding making new snow tracks to trick his father

00:08:08.445 --> 00:08:11.495
to think he went over the edge and his plan

00:08:11.495 --> 00:08:13.335
works. As Matthew looks over the presbi

00:08:13.335 --> 00:08:15.365
Henry pushes his father over

00:08:15.365 --> 00:08:17.395
fearing what he would do to his mother.

00:08:17.395 --> 00:08:19.765
The helicopter provides a moment of distraction

00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:22.735
which Henry uses to attack the kid. He wrestles his gun from his hand

00:08:22.735 --> 00:08:24.595
gaining the apprehend and pointed at him.

00:08:24.595 --> 00:08:26.635
Before we see that might be the most shocking

00:08:26.635 --> 00:08:29.125
moment in the entire series

00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:31.825
the kid transforms into an old disfigured man

00:08:31.825 --> 00:08:34.345
that lets out a terrifying shrek

00:08:34.345 --> 00:08:35.815
is thi the devil?

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:38.635
something else? or is it all in Henry's mind?

00:08:38.635 --> 00:08:40.585
the answer? there is non.

00:08:40.585 --> 00:08:42.505
and that's the point of the show

00:08:42.505 --> 00:08:44.685
Starting back in episode one were giving

00:08:44.685 --> 00:08:47.835
different perspectives of several key events and is up to us

00:08:47.835 --> 00:08:48.985
the viewer

00:08:48.985 --> 00:08:51.725
to piece everything together and make a judgment for

00:08:51.725 --> 00:08:54.095
ourselves. Think of it like being in a court

00:08:54.095 --> 00:08:57.065
in fact it's even a hint of that in episode 3

00:08:57.065 --> 00:08:59.195
at the unjust convention of Molly with the kids

00:08:59.195 --> 00:09:00.975
Warden Lacy, Henry Deaver, Alan Pangborn

00:09:00.975 --> 00:09:03.935
are the prosecution claiming that the kid is the devil

00:09:03.935 --> 00:09:05.475
Whereas the kid is the defense

00:09:05.475 --> 00:09:08.005
In fact, a whole episode is devoted to

00:09:08.005 --> 00:09:09.465
hearing his side of the story

00:09:09.465 --> 00:09:12.215
We as the viewer are the jury

00:09:12.215 --> 00:09:14.855
But as Henry says in his voice over a year later

00:09:14.855 --> 00:09:17.245
truth isn't the same as justice, justice is a line that

00:09:17.245 --> 00:09:19.595
sweaves and that's the same in real life.

00:09:19.595 --> 00:09:22.485
People who are guilty get off and some were

00:09:22.485 --> 00:09:25.605
innocent are sent to jail, it happens all the time.

00:09:25.605 --> 00:09:28.345
Which leads us to the question of reasonable doubt.

00:09:28.345 --> 00:09:31.365
At the very beginning of this episode we get an extended

00:09:31.365 --> 00:09:33.525
scene of Henry talking to the jury

00:09:33.525 --> 00:09:36.515
on the murder case of Lyann Chambers from episode 1

00:09:36.515 --> 00:09:38.495
the jury blurred here is us

00:09:38.495 --> 00:09:41.605
Henry is talking directly to us asking

00:09:41.605 --> 00:09:44.445
"How much doubt are we comfortable with?" because for him

00:09:44.445 --> 00:09:47.275
if someones life was on the line just like Lyann

00:09:47.275 --> 00:09:49.525
the lady who gets the life penalty

00:09:49.525 --> 00:09:52.525
He'd needs it etched in gold and sang by God himself.

00:09:52.525 --> 00:09:55.375
in this place into why warden Lacy wouldn't kill the kid

00:09:55.375 --> 00:09:57.065
and he even said it himself

00:09:57.065 --> 00:10:00.035
deep down he has his doubts. what if the kid

00:10:00.035 --> 00:10:02.955
wasn't evil and he was torturing this person by keeping him

00:10:02.955 --> 00:10:05.745
cooped up in this cage for years

00:10:05.745 --> 00:10:08.205
back in the way we have so much soad that when it's revealed

00:10:08.205 --> 00:10:10.285
Henry's been keeping the kid in the water tank

00:10:10.285 --> 00:10:12.105
the kid remarks

00:10:12.105 --> 00:10:14.975
"After awhile you forget which side of bars you're on"

00:10:14.975 --> 00:10:16.835
He's referring to the metaphor of prison

00:10:16.835 --> 00:10:18.665
Henry and Lacy have had to live

00:10:18.665 --> 00:10:21.365
not knowing the truth about the kid and the reasonable

00:10:21.365 --> 00:10:23.545
doubt that he could not be evil

00:10:23.545 --> 00:10:26.485
this is why he would struggle day and a day out

00:10:26.485 --> 00:10:28.845
until he kills himself or passes on the beton

00:10:28.845 --> 00:10:31.835
similar to what Lacy did. the kid even asks

00:10:31.835 --> 00:10:34.265
"how much longer are we going to keep doing this?"

00:10:34.265 --> 00:10:36.645
to which Henry response "i don't know"

00:10:36.645 --> 00:10:39.075
Henry doesn't have a plan because he doesn't know

00:10:39.075 --> 00:10:40.705
what to do and he doesn't know

00:10:40.705 --> 00:10:43.325
what to believe. He's struggling in his own

00:10:43.325 --> 00:10:46.165
prison of self doubt. So if you felt that the end

00:10:46.165 --> 00:10:49.115
of this episode that you were cheated you have every right to be

00:10:49.115 --> 00:10:52.155
there were countless loose sands and unanswered questions

00:10:52.155 --> 00:10:54.845
not to mention the lack of the climax

00:10:54.845 --> 00:10:57.365
but also understand that the ambiguous ending

00:10:57.365 --> 00:11:00.335
was the whole point of the show. It was an allegory for justice

00:11:00.335 --> 00:11:02.425
What would you do if the kid was on trial

00:11:02.425 --> 00:11:05.415
and you had to make the decision to sentence him to death?

00:11:05.415 --> 00:11:08.355
Would you? Is there enough reasonable doubt

00:11:08.355 --> 00:11:11.245
Or would you struggle like Henry and Lacy did?

00:11:11.245 --> 00:11:13.745
by having an unclear cut ending the show wonders would've likely given

00:11:13.745 --> 00:11:16.605
us a better more obvious ending

00:11:16.605 --> 00:11:18.795
at the expense of depriving us at a even more

00:11:18.795 --> 00:11:21.245
discussion that of justice

00:11:21.245 --> 00:11:24.055
Did i like the ending? Well first i hated it.

00:11:24.055 --> 00:11:26.115
but i slowly started to warm up to it

00:11:26.115 --> 00:11:27.795
